    "columns_2_aNpKMf": {
      "type": "columns-2",
      "blocks": {
        "text_qMM7Vf": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "parent_column": "right",
            "enlarge_text": false,
            "text": "<p>When you’re new to Tarot, it can seem like you have SO MUCH TO LEARN! You can drive yourself nuts trying to learn all the spreads, study multiple guidebooks, and learn “the right” meaning of each of the 78 cards in your Tarot deck!</p><p>To make matters worse, your guidebooks have different (and sometimes contradictory) card interpretations, there are a whole bunch of reading techniques, you’re getting bogged down in complex esoteric systems and language that’s more than a little “out there,” and can someone just show you how to make sense of the Tower card and the Ace of Wands, already?!<br/><br/><em><strong>I Get It. Because I Used To Feel Like That Too.</strong></em></p>"
          }
        },
        "image_McVeik": {
          "type": "image",
          "settings": {
